  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Modern food is calorie-dense and nutrient-sparse by design. The Mitigate pillar
    approaches nutrition through the lens of sourcing and quality, not just macros.
    The same protein gram from a grass-finished ribeye and a feedlot-CAFO chicken breast
    carry meaningfully different inflammatory, hormonal, and micronutrient profiles.
  </p>
  <p>
    We don't prescribe a single dietary ideology. We prescribe a sourcing standard:
    animals raised on their natural diet, minimal processing, no seed oils, real food first.
    The cohort workbook includes weekly nutrition anchors aligned to the 4M protocol.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ancestral Sourcing Standard</h3>
      <p>Grass-finished beef, pasture-raised pork and poultry, wild-caught seafood — the baseline sourcing criteria.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Organ Meat Integration</h3>
      <p>Liver, heart, and kidney are the most nutrient-dense foods available. Ancestral Supplements offers encapsulated forms for those who won't eat them whole.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Seed Oil Elimination</h3>
      <p>Canola, soybean, sunflower, safflower, and corn oils drive linoleic acid accumulation. Remove them entirely.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Affiliate Sourcing Network</h3>
